   "bodyText": "Photo by Javardh on Unsplash\n\nThere are some truths I\u2019ve circled for years like a wounded animal \u2014 afraid to speak them, afraid of what they\u2019d mean if I did. But healing begins where honesty starts, and for me, that begins here:\n\nI struggle to swallow what I now believe I can finally be proud of.\n\nBut even pride \u2014 if it\u2019s not anchored in humility \u2014 can mask pain. The pain I\u2019ve caused others. The damage left in my wake. And so, I offer this not as an excuse, but as a confession. One with its own altar.\n\n\u201cI knew it the moment I met You. And I\u2019m sorry it took me so long to catch up.\n\nI got stuck.\u201d\n\n\u2014 To God, from the prodigal in me\n\n\ud83c\udf00 This reel hit me like a freight train.\n\n\u2e3b\n\nUnlearning Myself: What God Is Teaching Me\n\nTransformation isn\u2019t a switch. It\u2019s a slow, daily turning \u2014 repentance in action. And these are the muscles I\u2019m rebuilding with God\u2019s help. Muscles that atrophied in addiction, arrogance, avoidance, and performance.\n\nI Struggled to See Past Myself\n\nI assumed everyone processed pain like I did. That silence was safe. That numbing was normal. But God has shown me the beauty in seeing others clearly \u2014 not just as extensions of me, but as His creation. People with their own needs, wiring, and wounds. I\u2019m learning to listen differently. Slowly. With grace.\n\n2. I Confused Whimsy for Worth\n\nFor a long time, I chased novelty and chaos as a form of comfort. I mistook excitement for intimacy and spontaneity for purpose. But whimsy untethered from wisdom wrecks homes and hearts. God is showing me that discipline and devotion are the true rhythm of love \u2014 not dopamine hits, but daily bread.\n\n3. I Am an Addict\n\nThere. I said it. Not to wear it like a name tag, but to expose it to the Light. Addiction in my life has been subtle \u2014 strategic, even. It let me perform while perishing inside. But naming it has given me a new frame:\n\n\u201cI am not my addiction. I am God\u2019s. And He has plans for my freedom.\u201d\n\n4. Intimacy Used to Feel Unsafe\n\nFor years, I was afraid to be truly seen. The moment closeness came, so did my fear. \u201cYou\u2019re not wanted,\u201d said the voice in my head. \u201cYou\u2019re not safe. Not lovable. Not worth keeping.\u201d\n\nBut God \u2014 Abba \u2014 has been rewriting that script. Intimacy with Him is healing intimacy with others. And now I know:\n\nVulnerability is not a liability \u2014 it\u2019s a vessel for love.\n\n5. Trust Is Built in Stillness\n\nGod isn\u2019t in the noise. He\u2019s in the whisper. In the quiet. In the waiting. And if I\u2019m honest, patience has never been my strong suit. But I\u2019m learning that trust is less about control and more about surrender.\n\nNot \u201cHow can I fix this?\u201d but \u201cGod, how can I follow You through this?\u201d\n\n\u2e3b\n\nWhat I See in Myself (Through God\u2019s Eyes)\n\n\u2022 A beloved son \u2014 scarred but sanctified\n\n\u2022 A man called to lead with tenderness, not toughness\n\n\u2022 A soul reclaiming purpose from pain\n\n\u2022 A vessel being shaped for healing, not hiding\n\n\u2022 Someone willing to sit in the fire until the gold shines through\n\n\u2e3b\n\nWhat I Want to Offer to the People I Love\n\n\u2022 Consistency, not chaos\n\n\u2022 Truth, not just transparency\n\n\u2022 Peace, not performance\n\n\u2022 Repentance, not rationalization\n\n\u2022 Support without smothering, presence without pressure\n\n\u2e3b\n\nSupporting the Ones I\u2019ve Hurt\n\nI don\u2019t just want to be different. I want to be dependable. And that means learning what safety feels like \u2014 not just for me, but for others.\n\nHere\u2019s what I\u2019m learning to offer:\n\n\u2022 Regulated presence. If I\u2019m anxious, I don\u2019t dump that on others. I bring it to God first.\n\n\u2022 Listening without defending. Even when I want to justify, I practice being still.\n\n\u2022 Owning my past. I don\u2019t pretend it didn\u2019t happen. I let it testify to how far God\u2019s brought me.\n\n\u2022 Seeking repair, not just relief.\n\n\u2022 Showing up. Over and over and over again.\n\n\u2e3b\n\nWhere I\u2019m Placing My Hope\n\nThis reel reminded me: recovery isn\u2019t just about sobriety. It\u2019s about surrender. And I\u2019m learning to surrender daily to:\n\n\u2022 God\u2019s timing\n\n\u2022 God\u2019s healing\n\n\u2022 God\u2019s mercy\n\n\u2022 God\u2019s discipline\n\n\u2022 God\u2019s purpose for my pain\n\n\u2e3b\n\nFinal Word\n\nTo the ones reading this who feel like they\u2019ve burned every bridge \u2014\n\nTo the ones who wear shame like skin \u2014\n\nTo the ones who wonder if healing is real \u2014\n\nLet me say this plainly:\n\nYou are not beyond redemption.\n\nThe same God who met me at my lowest is meeting you now.\n\nNot to condemn you. But to carry you. To call you home.\n\nHe\u2019s not in a rush. But He is near. And He is patient.\n\nAnd if you\u2019re willing to get unstuck, He\u2019ll walk you out.\n\nStep by step.\n\nDay by day.\n\nGrace by grace.\n\nThis is where my new chapter begins.\n\n\u2e3b\n\n\u2e3b",
