   "sourceName": "Substack",
   "sourceUrl": "https://stevepeeleii.substack.com/p/profolio-v1-real-accounts-real-backend",
   "wordCount": 300,
   "bodyText": "I have a folder on my computer called \"career stuff.\" Resumes from 2019, 2021, 2023. A \"master resume\" that's nine pages long. Cover letter templates with [COMPANY NAME] still in them.\n\nEvery time I needed to send something to someone, I'd open the folder, stare at it, and send the same generic PDF I'd sent last time. Tailoring felt like a second job.\n\nSo I built Profolio. And this week it grew up \u2014 v1 is live with real accounts and a real backend.\n\nThe concept: one private baseline. You log your projects with real metrics \u2014 not \"drove growth\" but \"pipeline +212% in two quarters.\" Your skills, your credentials, all in one place. Takes about two minutes per project once you're rolling.\n\nThen the part I actually care about: views. A view is a named slice of your baseline for a specific audience. \"For SaaS hiring managers\" gets all three projects and the cert. \"For consulting clients\" gets the two relevant projects and drops the education line. You pick what each audience sees, share it as a link, and that's the whole story they get.\n\nNothing is public until you share. The link opens a clean page \u2014 no account needed on their end. Your baseline stays private to your account.\n\nMy broader thinking: the resume is a 500-year-old format duct-taped to a world where everyone you talk to needs a different story. The answer was never \"more resumes.\" It's one source of truth, packaged per audience.\n\nFree to start \u2014 5 projects and 1 view, enough to know if it's useful. Pro is $29 once for unlimited everything. No subscription. I don't do subscriptions for tools.\n\nTry it if it makes sense: https://profolio-stevepeeles-projects.vercel.app/\n\nBuilt by SPIIX \u2014 the operating system for demand. See what I'm about at signalsbyspii.com.",
