   "title": "The first 10 minutes of soundcheck are the worst part of my gig",
   "excerpt": "The band is on stage. Twenty-four channels. Every fader is at zero and they're all looking at you. That first 10 minutes of soundcheck is the worst part of monitor engineering..",
   "publishedAt": "2026-10-12T12:11:46.429Z",
   "category": "music",
   "tags": [
    "gigs",
    "performance"
   ],
   "sourceName": "Substack",
   "sourceUrl": "https://stevepeeleii.substack.com/p/the-first-10-minutes-of-soundcheck",
   "wordCount": 324,
   "bodyText": "The band is on stage. Twenty-four channels. Every fader is at zero and they're all looking at you.\n\nThat first 10 minutes of soundcheck is the worst part of monitor engineering. Not the mixing \u2014 the mixing is fun. It's the starting-from-nothing. You know roughly where everything goes, but you're building it live, under pressure, while the drummer asks for \"more me\" in a wedge that isn't rung out yet.\n\nHere's the thing: the starting points barely change. Kick drum? HPF at 40, cut the 400Hz mud, 4:1 compression. Every time. Lead vocal? HPF at 100, de-ess at 6k, 3:1, and it's the loudest thing in every wedge. Every time. Snare? You already know.\n\nSo I built Monitor Mix Cheat to do the obvious part. Paste the input list. Pick the venue \u2014 club, theater, outdoor, church, bar \u2014 because the room changes the advice. Pick wedges or IEMs, because those are different sports. Out comes a per-channel cheat sheet: HPF, EQ moves with actual frequencies, compression starting points, starting levels, and the notes I'd tell a junior engineer (\"vox is king, build every mix around it\").\n\nIt's editable \u2014 click any cell and change it, because your ears beat my table. Copy-as-text for your show notes. Print to PDF for the dog-eared binder.\n\nMy broader thinking: live sound runs on tribal knowledge that lives in people's heads and dies when they retire. Encoding the boring, repeatable parts into tools isn't replacing engineers \u2014 it's giving them a head start so they can spend soundcheck actually listening instead of guessing.\n\nFree to try right now. $19 one-time when I put the paywall up. No subscription \u2014 I don't do subscriptions for tools.\n\nTry it if it makes sense: https://monitor-mix-cheat-stevepeeles-projects.vercel.app/\n\nBuilt by SPIIX \u2014 the operating system for demand. See what I'm about at signalsbyspii.com.\n\nWhat's your most controversial monitor starting point? I'm collecting corrections \u2014 reply and tell me where my table is wrong.",
